{"id": "EUVD-2026-102525", "enisaUuid": "d1a679d3-38f6-324e-807b-acb818c0955a", "description": "libmodplug through 0.8.9.1 contains a heap-based out-of-bounds write in CSoundFile::ReadDSM() in src/load_dsm.cpp because nPat is never checked against MAX_PATTERNS. Attackers can supply a crafted DSM file with over 240 PATT chunks or a wrapping patt_len value to corrupt heap memory and crash the consuming process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:33:42", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libmodplug-dsm-pattern-oob-write", "https://github.com/Konstanty/libmodplug/blob/d1b97ed0020bc620a059d3675d1854b40bd2608d/src/load_dsm.cpp#L130-L139", "https://github.com/Konstanty/libmodplug", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libmodplug-through-0.8.9.1-heap-out-of-bounds-write-via-csoundfile-readdsm"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rxvf-jg5h-5fv5", "CVE-2026-111270"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04ebe460-060c-3791-b160-5b614e63bac4", "product": {"name": "libmodplug", "vendor": {"name": "Konstanty Bialkowski"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.8.9.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5602dd72-8561-3233-96d6-87f9e6e84130", "vendor": {"name": "Konstanty Bialkowski"}}], "isExploited": false}